## To release a new version, edit the version in the two lines below and nothing else.
## |cRRGGBB...|r in Title and Author colours them in the in-game add-on list; the version
## is read back through that markup, so it can sit inside or outside the colour.
## The settings panel takes its version from ## Title; the name itself is fixed in Main.lua.
## Title: |cFF69B4PB's CyrodiilAlert|r 2.5.2
## Author: |cFF69B4PinkBanther|r
## Description: Watches your alliance's holdings in Cyrodiil on a timer and says it in chat when one comes under attack -- red while it is being attacked, blue when the attack is beaten off, yellow when it is lost. The name of the keep, outpost or town is in every line. Checking interval and repeat time are settings; the default is every 5 seconds, with a standing attack repeated after a minute. Optionally also reports in green when a fight starts at a holding another alliance owns -- by default only where your own alliance has siege standing there, which is as close as the client can get to "we are the ones attacking". Alerts can also be drawn on screen, shortened, with the typeface, size, position and which alerts appear there all adjustable; every alert's colour can be set separately for chat and for the screen. A rough campaign summary -- holdings, scores and what is being fought over -- can also be kept in a corner of the screen, with its own switch, size and position. Elder Scrolls changing hands are reported with the name of the player carrying them, which is the one thing in AvA the game will name. Everything it says goes into a window of its own by default, sized and placed where you want it, so it never fills the chat window. An overview map of the whole of Cyrodiil can be kept in a corner -- keeps in their owners' colours, attacks, scrolls, Volendrung and you -- drawn on its own, so it runs alongside a minimap add-on. Settings panel, or /pbalert.
## Version: 2.5.2
## APIVersion: 101050 101051
## OptionalDependsOn: LibHarvensAddonSettings>=20106
## SavedVariables: PBsCyrodiilAlert_Data

lang/strings.lua
lang/$(language).lua

Main.lua
Hud.lua
Map.lua
Settings.lua

